BT /F2 13 Tf 56.00 771.89 Td (6. Information security and two-factor authentication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 739.89 Td (Access to enterprise applications requires two-factor authentication. The second factor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 724.89 Td (is a six-digit one-time code delivered to the employee's registered email address. Codes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 709.89 Td (expire after ten minutes and may be attempted at most five times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 684.89 Td (Employees must not forward verification codes, approve authentication prompts they did) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 669.89 Td (not initiate, or reuse a code across sessions. If a code arrives without an active login) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 56.00 654.89 Td (attempt, report it to the security team immediately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 70.00 633.89 Td (- Use a unique passphrase for each enterprise account and store it in the approved) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 70.00 618.89 Td (  password manager.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 70.00 599.89 Td (- Lock the screen whenever leaving a workstation unattended.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 70.00 580.89 Td (- Report suspected phishing to the security team without clicking any link.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 30 Td (Employee Handbook - demonstration sample - page 7 of 10) Tj ET
endstream
